Yeah, exactly.

07:02.760 --> 07:13.540
We have to stop looking at code as a sequential list of instructions that ruthlessly overwrite each other and start looking at it as an irreversible, geometrically growing structure.

07:13.760 --> 07:18.720
Okay, let's start with that shift, specifically looking at what the text calls the parenthesis illusion.

07:19.460 --> 07:28.420
There's a surprising fact pointed out early in the monograph that blew my mind a little bit simply because it is so obvious yet completely invisible until someone points it out.

07:28.500 --> 07:30.080
