17:11.680 --> 17:16.360
The compiler knows exactly what rules and inputs were used to generate that deleted data.

17:16.560 --> 17:21.440
So the computer doesn't crash from memory overload, it just intelligently manages how it remembers,

17:21.440 --> 17:28.260
shifting the heavy raw data out, but keeping the irrefutable mathematical proof of the journey.

17:28.720 --> 17:34.120
So it's the difference between throwing away all your tax receipts into a fire, because you already filed your return,

